 "brief_issues": [
  "No 'default powers' heading exists in Their powers. The four defaults sit under three headings: Holding their ground (Unbreakable footing, own recoil), Material limit suspended (Things keep their form) and Absorbed (Air resistance absorbed). So 'move to the default powers' has no target. Proposal: give Safe passenger its own eyebrow ('People they throw or catch') before 'Absorbed', and list it in the intro hint (app.html:325) and the summary line as a default.",
  "The brief puts the wrong words on the switch. 'puts no load on them; they float as if falling' is in passengerText (app.html:1304). The switch label (app.html:347) says 'so his push puts no g-force on them. Air drag in flight and the landing stay real.' Both need the new 'manageable push, spread through them, at the launch, in the air and when they land' wording, and the chip and the 'covers only his push, not the air' clause (1295, 1308) too.",
  "'The powers-off fixture keeps passing' can't hold as written. test/powers-off-cases.js:92 runs the planner with safePassenger:true, and under PR3 exactly 8 fixture keys change (plan|throw|person|inf|…|5), with main's drag hazard at about 39,700 kg-force going to never. Decision: a test-side shim in powers.js part 1 that restores main's passenger rule for those keys only, plus an assertion that only they differ. Verified: all 584 person or Safe-passenger cases match under the shim.",
  "Save marker risk. STATUS.md:14 tells the owner to republish once PR1 (#31) merges. If that happens before PR3 is live, saves carry saveV:2 with safePassenger:false (the old default), and the brief's rule would read them as a choice. Decision: bump the marker to saveV:3 in PR3; the Safe passenger migration runs on <3, the 3,007 kg one stays on <2, and the shots.js:316-317 expectations move. Otherwise record that no republish happened in between.",
  "The landing's blast, crater and quake are not covered. Energy taken back implies no landing blast for a person with the switch on (throwBlast land part). This doesn't move the ceiling, but at a 1e9 kg dial the windows preset moves from 1.78e6 to 3.88e8 kg-force and houses from 1.61e6 to 2.41e8. The page's crater and quake line for a person past about 9.6 km/s should say 'taken back'. Proposal: include it, guarded, and confirm in the physics review.",
  "The landing's split rests on a reading: a spread push versus a gentle stop. landShake stops the person in L/v (L = 0.56 m): 0.031 s, about 59 g on average, 2.51 mm/s at 5 m at the least effort. That fits the switch's 'spread through them' mechanism and Soft landing's precedent. If 'manageable force' were read as a gentle stop (1.5 g), the pulse would be 1.2 s at 0.0013 mm/s, plaster would never crack, and the ceiling would move to the boom. Recommend the brief's reading; state it in the card and README.",
  "Heating in flight isn't covered. Safe passenger covers the push, the drag and the landing, not heat. With Things keep their form off and a person past about Mach 3, the page says the object 'would melt or burn away' (app.html:1586 area). The landing text must not also say 'unharmed' there.",
  "Catch with a person: 'covers where the person lands' also reaches the Catch tab. Its miss callout (app.html:2928) and the duo harm 'the throw hits the ground X away' (duoFacts) need a decision. Proposal: the callout says they come down unharmed with the energy taken back; keep 'hits-ground' as a failed throw.",
  "The figures at 3,000 kg differ slightly from the brief's (written at 3,007 kg):\n- Least effort with the switch on is 3,342 kg-force, not 3,350.\n- Its ceiling is plaster, onset 26,991 kg-force (search use 27,052), so 'about 27,000'.\n- With the switch off, least 333 and ceiling use 334 kg-force, not 335 (onset 333.4).\n- All-out: 80.8 m/s, range 668 m.\nThe 1.4 m plaster reach (1.36 m) and the 16 m fall (16.5 m) hold.",
  "The brief overstates the drag change. At the default (Air resistance absorbed 100%), main with the switch on already gives 3,342 / 27,000 kg-force: drag is zero, so the 'New: on' row comes only from the default flip. The drag rule matters only below 100%, for example the all-four-off row: ceiling passenger at 39,700 kg-force becomes none, least 3,929 kg-force.",
  "Flipping the default changes the Catch tab with a person, a change the brief doesn't call out. With the switch off, even a 10 m lob is past the ride limits (2.28 g over 0.58 s, against a 1.5 g limit), so the duo search's passenger harm disappears by default. No test covers a person in Catch.",
  "Research data contradicts the ruling. comic_passenger_drag_g is labelled '(not removed by safe passenger once released)', with notes 'safe passenger stops when he lets go'. Relabel it and rebuild data.js.",
  "shots.js POWERS_OFF lacks safePassenger:false and a marker, so after PR3 the 'powers off' page comparisons run with Safe passenger on. Results don't move, because no case uses a person; fix it for intent."
 ],
